librqbit-dualstack-sockets, vendored for Marquee

Upstream: https://github.com/ikatson/librqbit-dualstack-sockets, commit
e2f221ca745c25c7790abb593ed260ce5a499fa1 (from the package's
.cargo_vcs_info.json), published to crates.io as librqbit-dualstack-sockets
0.7.0. Copyright 2025 Igor Katson. Licensed under the Apache License, Version
2.0: LICENSE is upstream's header as the registry package ships it,
LICENSE-APACHE-2.0 the full text (copied from vendor/librqbit). Upstream ships
no NOTICE file of its own.

What was taken: src/, README.md, LICENSE, Cargo.toml.orig and the Cargo.toml
published to crates.io for 0.7.0, plus an empty [workspace] table.

Marquee changes (the changed spot carries a "Marquee fork" comment):

- src/bind_device.rs: `BindDevice::bind_sref` binds by interface index
  (`bind_device_by_index_v4` / `_v6`) on iOS and tvOS as on macOS. Upstream
  gates that to macOS only, so the iOS and tvOS builds fell to socket2's
  `bind_device`, which exists only on Linux, Android and Fuchsia, and failed
  to compile (E0599).
